  "about": "Prints joined into aggressor events, checked by the runtime (tessera-market orderflow::big_trades) and the desk alike. A print is [t, price, size, side, order?] as on the wire (t in UTC nanoseconds, side 1 buy / -1 sell / 0 unknown, order the aggressor order's key when the feed names it). An event is [t, vwap, size, side, prints, levels, orders]. Consecutive prints join when they are the same order (the same key when both name one; without keys, the same time and side, and without a side also the same price), or when another order on the same side continues the event: at most 5 ms after its last print, at a price that does not retreat and is at most 2 ticks beyond its extreme. Those events are the default grouping, both settings on. A case's settings list the events under the other groupings: joinOrders off joins prints only by the 5 ms chain, reachLimit off lets a continuation reach any number of ticks, and both off joins by the chain alone. Prints without a side join only at one price and time under every grouping.",
